{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Report (from a rebar client)\nA Rebar CLI quirk treated `create task --help` as a literal task and created an accidental placeholder ticket.\n\n## Observed\nRunning `rebar create task --help` (an attempt to view help for the create-task command) does NOT print help — instead the parser consumes `--help` as the positional title argument, so a ticket titled `--help` (a placeholder) is actually CREATED.\n\n## Expected\n`create task --help` (and `--help`/`-h` on any create subcommand) should print the command's usage/help and create NOTHING. Help must never be interpreted as ticket content.\n\n## Impact\nAccidental placeholder tickets pollute the store and require cleanup; the write side-effect on a help request is surprising and violates least-astonishment.\n\n## Notes / possible cause\nThe create command path likely reads the first positional as the title before any --help interception. Compare with the argparse standardization landed for the write commands (claim/transition, ticket fd48-7a80-33e9-4400): --help there is served byte-exact by the top-level dispatcher and never reaches the handler. The create path may bypass that dispatcher help interception, or accept a bare positional that swallows `--help`. Needs repro + root-cause.\n\n## Repro\n1. `rebar create task --help`\n2. Observe: no help text; a new ticket titled `--help` is created (verify via `rebar list`).\n\n## Confirmed root cause\n`rebar._cli.main` only treats `--help`/`-h` as a help request when it is the FIRST\ntoken after the subcommand (`rest[0]`): the guard is\n`if rest and rest[0] in (\"--help\", \"-h\") and sub not in _HIDDEN_ALIASES:`. For\n`create task --help`, `rest == [\"task\", \"--help\"]`, so `rest[0] == \"task\"` and the guard\nis skipped; dispatch falls through to `composer.create_cli`, whose hand-rolled parser\nreads `rest[0]` as the ticket type and `rest[1]` (`--help`) as the title, then performs\nthe CREATE write. The commands that \"own\" their `--help` (review-plan, workflow, audit, …)\nare intercepted earlier and are unaffected; the bug hits the fall-through write commands.\n\n## Fix\nIn `rebar._cli.main`, recognise `--help`/`-h` appearing ANYWHERE in `rest` before a `--`\nterminator (not only at `rest[0]`) as a help request for a routable subcommand, matching\nargparse semantics (help short-circuits regardless of position). A `_wants_help(rest)`\nhelper scans `rest`, stopping at `--`. A `_help_requested(sub, rest)` wrapper makes this\nfamily-aware: nested-dispatch families (the `bridge` group) own their children's help, so\nthey honour only a LEADING `--help`/`-h` (a later flag belongs to a child such as\n`bridge preview --help`, served by `bridge_cli`) — keeping `bridge --help` identical to\n`help bridge`. Every other command uses the any-position scan. `_HIDDEN_ALIASES` stays\nexcluded and the earlier own-their-help intercepts are untouched. Help serves the\nbyte-exact pinned usage via the existing `_emit_subcommand_help(sub)` and performs NO write.\n\n## Testing\n- Regression: `main([\"create\", \"task\", \"--help\"])` returns 0, prints the create usage to\n  stdout, and creates NO ticket (store unchanged).\n- Position parity: `-h` in a later position and `--help` after a title are also honoured.\n- `_wants_help`/`_help_requested` unit contracts: any-position scan for leaf commands,\n  leading-only for the `bridge` family, `--` terminator respected.\n- Unchanged: `rebar create task \"real title\"` still creates; `bridge --help` == `help\n  bridge`; `bridge preview --help` shows preview usage; unknown subcommand still errors.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `rebar create task --help` prints the create usage (exit 0) and creates NO ticket.\n- [x] `--help`/`-h` anywhere before a `--` terminator triggers subcommand help for routable\n      write commands (create/edit/comment/link/…), not just at `rest[0]`.\n- [x] The `bridge` nested-dispatch family keeps its own help: `bridge --help` equals\n      `help bridge` and `bridge preview --help` shows preview usage.\n- [x] Commands that own their own `--help` and unknown-subcommand handling are unchanged.\n- [x] A regression test (tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py)\n      covers the no-write help behavior and the `_wants_help`/`_help_requested` contracts;\n      bridge parity is covered by tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py and\n      test_bridge_cli_heldout.py."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787133184396009001,"uuid":"cbb7ccaa-9adb-469e-99fe-1d3d741916d0"}